WEBVTT

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.403
I heard you calling
for help, Suiryu.

00:00:11.658 --> 00:00:13.284
You fought well on your own.

00:00:15.161 --> 00:00:16.788
Let me handle the rest.

00:00:26.839 --> 00:00:28.508
I know that head...

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.942
Through the once tranquil town

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:48.361
A thunderous roar peals forth

00:00:48.444 --> 00:00:52.281
Watch out! Freak out! Monsters!

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:55.284
Who ts going to take the lead

00:00:55.326 --> 00:00:57.787
When we destroy the evil ones?

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:02.583
Destruction, contusion...
Loosen up!

00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:04.627
We know, We are...

00:01:04.794 --> 00:01:07.295
HEROES!

00:01:07.296 --> 00:01:09.048
Why were you

00:01:09.173 --> 00:01:11.342
born of evil?

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:13.428
If you wish to know

00:01:13.553 --> 00:01:15.805
I shall tell!

00:01:15.972 --> 00:01:21.853
This night the punching fist
of glorious justice

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.314
Will shatter your fate apart!

00:01:26.607 --> 00:01:31.195
That word exists for you
and you alone

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.867
Raise your silent fist
to the sky!

00:01:35.992 --> 00:01:40.538
The apostle bears
the weight of solitude

00:01:40.663 --> 00:01:46.836
For a peace not filled
with hatred

00:01:46.961 --> 00:01:50.173
He must fight!

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:03.770
A hero?

00:02:04.187 --> 00:02:05.521
A goddam hero?!

00:02:05.938 --> 00:02:10.193
More like some puny runt
out to make a name for himself!

00:02:10.359 --> 00:02:14.572
THE TROUBLES OF THE STRONGEST

00:02:15.198 --> 00:02:16.324
You're nothing but...

00:02:16.616 --> 00:02:17.700
You're...

00:02:22.038 --> 00:02:24.582
Wait, do I know you?
Have we met?

00:02:24.832 --> 00:02:25.792
Shut your face!

00:02:26.292 --> 00:02:29.170
This time, Bakuzan #he Monster

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.048
will rain down upon you
a full course of death blows!

00:02:32.548 --> 00:02:37.011
Art of the Darkness Hell Killer:
Demon Sweeper Low Kick!

00:02:41.682 --> 00:02:42.642
He got you guys, too...

00:02:43.476 --> 00:02:46.270
That you're still standing
is impressive,

00:02:46.521 --> 00:02:48.272
but by now, you've realized

00:02:48.397 --> 00:02:50.149
the unimaginable difference
in our strength.

00:02:50.942 --> 00:02:53.236
Bear Killer Mid Kick!

00:02:54.737 --> 00:02:57.198
/s he protecting the injured?

00:02:57.448 --> 00:02:59.242
Protect yourself first!

00:02:59.492 --> 00:03:01.410
Carnage Punch!

00:03:04.372 --> 00:03:07.583
You've got one last chance
to apologize for our match!

00:03:10.586 --> 00:03:12.255
Tch! This guy's no fun.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.090
He must have gone into shock.

00:03:14.507 --> 00:03:15.633
Time to end this!

00:03:15.925 --> 00:03:18.427
Those scrawny nothings
have to go too!

00:03:18.553 --> 00:03:20.221
Hellbringin' Hand Chop!

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:21.848
Darn it, I just can't remember.

00:03:27.854 --> 00:03:29.397
Who was this guy?

00:03:29.981 --> 00:03:30.982
Eh, whatever.

00:03:34.944 --> 00:03:37.196
That really sucked for you...

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.031
After winning
the tournament and all?

00:03:39.949 --> 00:03:43.119
Well, I defeated the monsters,
so maybe next time won't be so bad.

00:03:43.411 --> 00:03:44.912
Okay, yeah...

00:03:45.204 --> 00:03:47.331
Thank you for saving me...

00:03:48.124 --> 00:03:50.960
Wh-Who are you really?

00:03:51.878 --> 00:03:54.338
I'm Saitama. A hero.

00:03:54.881 --> 00:03:55.840
Saitama?

00:03:56.174 --> 00:03:59.427
So you fought in the tournament
under an alias?

00:03:59.802 --> 00:04:00.761
Uh...oops.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.306
What were you doing here?

00:04:03.973 --> 00:04:06.100
Was this all some plan
of the Hero Association's?

00:04:06.642 --> 00:04:09.228
No. I wanted to
experience martial arts.

00:04:09.979 --> 00:04:11.147
And win the prize money.

00:04:12.148 --> 00:04:14.609
There's this guy calling himself
a "Hero Hunter."

00:04:15.359 --> 00:04:17.320
They say
he's a martial arts master...

00:04:17.945 --> 00:04:19.655
...SO I sort of got interested.

00:04:19.947 --> 00:04:22.575
I see. You were looking
for ways to counter him?

00:04:22.992 --> 00:04:25.494
Well, I wouldn't exactly say that.

00:04:26.537 --> 00:04:28.998
I just happened across
an entry ticket.

00:04:29.165 --> 00:04:30.333
More specifically...

00:04:32.627 --> 00:04:33.586
...| was bored.

00:04:34.587 --> 00:04:36.088
You were bored?

00:04:36.339 --> 00:04:38.799
Thanks to you, though,
I'm still alive.

00:04:39.592 --> 00:04:41.636
Sorry I didn't get here sooner.

00:04:41.969 --> 00:04:43.304
Saitama!

00:04:44.597 --> 00:04:46.390
You shouldn't go out there.

00:04:46.515 --> 00:04:49.310
Some dangerous group
called the "Monster Association"

00:04:49.393 --> 00:04:50.853
is on a rampage outside.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:51.854
You serious?

00:04:51.979 --> 00:04:52.855
Yeah.

00:04:52.939 --> 00:04:56.317
Seems they're able to turn
humans into monsters.

00:04:57.151 --> 00:04:59.278
Bakuzan, who you just beat,
was one of them.

00:04:59.362 --> 00:05:00.988
Remember? From your second match.

00:05:01.781 --> 00:05:03.366
So that's who he was?

00:05:03.532 --> 00:05:06.744
I mean, I can't remember
every opponent I punch.

00:05:07.203 --> 00:05:11.499
Anyway, it's dangerous right now,
so we should lay low.

00:05:11.999 --> 00:05:14.043
Goketsu is still somewhere nearby.

00:05:14.543 --> 00:05:15.544
Goketsu?

00:05:15.836 --> 00:05:18.631
Yeah. He's another monster
I'd avoid.

00:05:19.423 --> 00:05:22.885
Nothing I could do had
any effect on him.

00:05:23.886 --> 00:05:25.930
That kind of strength
should be illegal.

00:05:28.808 --> 00:05:31.102
When my repairs are done
I must return at once.

00:05:31.686 --> 00:05:32.853
Even if he caught me off-guard,

00:05:32.937 --> 00:05:34.897
a monster that can beat me
with one punch...

00:05:36.107 --> 00:05:37.942
...nust not be allowed to survive.

00:05:38.484 --> 00:05:41.988
I need to gather the Class S heroes
and Master Saitama,

00:05:42.363 --> 00:05:43.614
then strike together!

00:05:44.824 --> 00:05:46.409
So he's that strong?

00:05:46.492 --> 00:05:48.995
Even with the most
meticulous preparation,

00:05:49.078 --> 00:05:50.371
who knows if he can be beat?

00:05:50.871 --> 00:05:51.831
I see.

00:05:52.498 --> 00:05:54.417
So, where'd this monster go?

00:05:54.792 --> 00:05:56.669
What? That way, but...

00:05:57.211 --> 00:06:00.006
Oh... So all that noise earlier
was him, huh?

00:06:00.923 --> 00:06:01.632
I'll check it out.

00:06:01.757 --> 00:06:03.759
What? No!

00:06:03.843 --> 00:06:05.886
Weren't you listening?
I'm trying to warn you!

00:06:06.595 --> 00:06:08.306
I heard you. And?

00:06:08.431 --> 00:06:10.266
You still don't get it!

00:06:10.433 --> 00:06:13.561
He was once
a preeminent martial artist.

00:06:13.644 --> 00:06:16.188
He's no ordinary fighter!
You'll be killed for sure!

00:06:16.272 --> 00:06:18.441
Whoa, a master of martial arts, eh?

00:06:18.858 --> 00:06:19.734
Perfect.

00:06:19.817 --> 00:06:21.444
It might help my indigestion.

00:06:22.361 --> 00:06:25.489
Hey... You're injured.
Take it easy.

00:06:26.073 --> 00:06:27.283
I'm not letting go.

00:06:27.491 --> 00:06:29.076
I won't let you
throw your life away

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.119
when I owe you mine!

00:06:50.181 --> 00:06:51.807
I couldn't stop him!

00:06:56.479 --> 00:07:01.233
I finally saw what a hero,
a true hero, can be!

00:07:02.485 --> 00:07:04.445
He shouldn't die now...

00:07:04.862 --> 00:07:08.908
He's destined to save
many, many more people...

00:07:21.045 --> 00:07:22.129
Oh, by the way...

00:07:22.254 --> 00:07:24.423
There's something
I forgot to mention.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.426
That thing about me lying
to get into the tournament...

00:07:27.718 --> 00:07:29.178
Could we keep it a secret?

00:07:32.223 --> 00:07:34.308
Was Goketsu tough?

00:07:35.684 --> 00:07:38.479
When they only take one punch,
it's kinda hard to compare.

00:07:39.188 --> 00:07:40.856
I want to ask you something.

00:07:41.399 --> 00:07:42.358
Yeah?

00:07:42.483 --> 00:07:45.361
I don't know if I can
overcome my fear,

00:07:45.653 --> 00:07:47.196
but I'd like to try.

00:07:47.863 --> 00:07:50.699
Do you think I could become...
a hero?

00:07:50.866 --> 00:07:51.325
No idea.

00:07:51.659 --> 00:07:52.618
Huh?

00:07:52.993 --> 00:07:53.702
But you know...

00:07:54.745 --> 00:07:57.540
If I became one, maybe anyone can?

00:07:58.416 --> 00:08:00.209
It's natural to be afraid
at the start.

00:08:00.918 --> 00:08:03.295
Before I got too strong,
I was afraid too.

00:08:04.588 --> 00:08:06.549
A hero who's too strong?

00:08:07.299 --> 00:08:08.884
Doesn't sound too bad.

00:08:09.927 --> 00:08:12.471
Can I ask you another question,
Saitama?

00:08:12.721 --> 00:08:13.722
Sure.

00:08:14.181 --> 00:08:15.433
Could I be your disciple?

00:08:18.185 --> 00:08:19.228
Absolutely not.

00:08:22.064 --> 00:08:23.149
Darnn it...

00:08:23.399 --> 00:08:25.401
His whole body's covered in spikes.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.069
How do I fight him?

00:08:27.695 --> 00:08:31.073
— Prisoner! Don't use your hands!
— Use your ball and chain!

00:08:31.198 --> 00:08:32.950
Yeah, nail him with your chain!

00:08:34.535 --> 00:08:37.288
Thank you for
the enthusiastic support, young people!

00:08:37.413 --> 00:08:39.665
Later, I'll shower you
with kisses of gratitude,

00:08:39.748 --> 00:08:41.417
but for now,
evacuate the rooftop!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.961
It's no good, he can't hear us.

00:08:44.336 --> 00:08:47.089
Does he have to fight
completely naked?

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:51.177
You fresh-faced boys cheering me on
without regard for your own safety...

00:08:51.677 --> 00:08:53.596
Your love will not go unrewarded!

00:08:54.263 --> 00:08:55.431
Ah! Love!

00:08:56.348 --> 00:08:58.517
Thats it...
That's the answer.

00:08:58.851 --> 00:09:01.896
/can accept the pain
with love so deep...

00:09:03.355 --> 00:09:05.274
...there will be nothing
left to fear!

00:09:07.443 --> 00:09:09.278
Angel Hug...!

00:09:16.327 --> 00:09:19.538
He keeps staring at us...
with blood all over him.

00:09:21.457 --> 00:09:23.792
Hello? Puri-puri Prisoner speaking.

00:09:24.627 --> 00:09:25.586
What?

00:09:25.753 --> 00:09:28.964
It broke into my comfy cozy home
and stole my honeys?!

00:09:30.216 --> 00:09:31.884
Where is this monster now?

00:09:33.427 --> 00:09:34.386
They're gone?

00:09:35.304 --> 00:09:38.516
Yeah... They all left together...
maybe 30 minutes ago.

00:09:39.475 --> 00:09:43.062
They came all at once, went crazy,
then left all at once?

00:09:44.647 --> 00:09:46.190
What were they up to?

00:09:47.233 --> 00:09:48.317
Darnn it.

00:09:48.484 --> 00:09:50.444
How I miss such a huge disaster?

00:09:50.736 --> 00:09:53.155
The other heroes
were out here fighting.

00:09:53.364 --> 00:09:54.573
What was I thinking?

00:09:55.157 --> 00:09:57.493
I cant call myself a hero
If! dont defeat monsters.

00:09:59.828 --> 00:10:00.538
Wait a Sec...

00:10:01.497 --> 00:10:05.501
I dont tight monsters because
I want to be called a hero.

00:10:06.335 --> 00:10:08.879
I might have forgotten
something important.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.507
Like the reason
why I became a hero...

00:10:13.008 --> 00:10:15.427
I started out just having fun.

00:10:16.095 --> 00:10:19.223
But since joining
the Hero Association,

00:10:19.348 --> 00:10:20.558
I've been so bored.

00:10:21.475 --> 00:10:24.103
That "hero hunter" guy
got me curious again.

00:10:24.645 --> 00:10:27.606
That's why I entered
the martial arts tournament.

00:10:28.941 --> 00:10:29.900
But...

00:10:30.317 --> 00:10:32.319
Against Suiryu and the others,

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:35.614
even a monster who was
a master martial artist,

00:10:35.864 --> 00:10:37.533
I didn't really feel anything.

00:10:38.492 --> 00:10:40.369
And I didn't get anything
out of it.

00:10:41.453 --> 00:10:42.538
Saitama?

00:10:45.541 --> 00:10:46.542
King?

00:10:48.419 --> 00:10:50.462
You sure it's safe to be out here?

00:10:51.714 --> 00:10:55.968
Well, I heard the alarms,
but it's all quiet now.

00:10:56.218 --> 00:10:58.012
Why're you looking so down?

00:10:58.679 --> 00:11:01.056
You know...
Got a lot on my mind.

00:11:01.807 --> 00:11:02.766
I get it.

00:11:03.017 --> 00:11:05.603
But you're still young,
so you can't give up.

00:11:06.186 --> 00:11:07.229
King...

00:11:07.521 --> 00:11:09.940
Besides, it might grow back.

00:11:10.065 --> 00:11:10.899
And there's treatments—

00:11:11.025 --> 00:11:11.984
Wait, hold on!

00:11:12.109 --> 00:11:13.902
That's not what
I'm talking about!

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:16.447
It's more of a big picture thing.

00:11:16.572 --> 00:11:20.451
Being down isn't like you.
You're always so strong.

00:11:21.118 --> 00:11:24.371
Well, I'm not going to be
getting any stronger.

00:11:24.622 --> 00:11:25.247
What?

00:11:25.372 --> 00:11:27.124
I've become too strong.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.586
No matter who I fight,
I don't feel anything.

00:11:30.961 --> 00:11:32.296
I gain nothing from it.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.507
There's nothing I can learn
from anyone.

00:11:35.883 --> 00:11:40.346
But isn't having that much strength
really awesome?

00:11:40.596 --> 00:11:41.555
King...

00:11:41.847 --> 00:11:43.891
Not having any room to grow

00:11:44.099 --> 00:11:47.478
means that I can't enjoy
the process of growing.

00:11:49.021 --> 00:11:50.939
No matter how many monsters
I defeat,

00:11:51.607 --> 00:11:54.568
inside, I'm bored out of my mind.

00:11:57.446 --> 00:12:00.115
I never thought being a hero
could be so lonesome.

00:12:00.449 --> 00:12:02.534
You feel lonely, Saitama?

00:12:02.951 --> 00:12:03.786
Guess so.

00:12:03.869 --> 00:12:06.288
There's a ballroom dance school
near the station

00:12:06.413 --> 00:12:07.665
you could check out.

00:12:07.915 --> 00:12:09.124
Why would I do that?

00:12:09.416 --> 00:12:11.460
If you're lonely,
you could make friends.

00:12:11.919 --> 00:12:14.797
No, that's not quite
what I mean.

00:12:15.047 --> 00:12:15.756
Then what?

00:12:15.839 --> 00:12:17.424
It's hard to explain...

00:12:17.675 --> 00:12:18.634
I'm not interested,

00:12:19.134 --> 00:12:21.011
and I don't have much time
these days.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:24.973
Once things settle down, what about
a trip to change things up?

00:12:25.391 --> 00:12:26.475
A trip?

00:12:27.851 --> 00:12:30.062
There's no place
I particularly want to go...

00:12:30.979 --> 00:12:32.231
Good grief...

00:12:32.648 --> 00:12:34.942
You're bored and want
some excitement,

00:12:35.025 --> 00:12:37.486
but you won't take on
any challenges.

00:12:38.278 --> 00:12:40.280
There was a time
I felt that way too.

00:12:41.281 --> 00:12:42.658
Listen to me, Saitama.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:44.827
Life is a journey to nowhere.

00:12:45.452 --> 00:12:47.204
If you want a change of scenery,

00:12:47.329 --> 00:12:49.415
you need to find
your own way there.

00:12:49.873 --> 00:12:51.542
You sure you've been
on a trip before?

00:12:52.126 --> 00:12:54.670
Saitama, seems to me
you're mistaking

00:12:54.753 --> 00:12:57.589
getting strong
for reaching your destination.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:03.345
I doubt the path of becoming a hero
ends so easily.

00:13:04.388 --> 00:13:07.933
Is this a lecture? It's not like
you're some veteran hero.

00:13:08.475 --> 00:13:12.688
It's inherently wrong to seek
satisfaction from fighting.

00:13:13.188 --> 00:13:16.483
Battling with great courage
and benefitting society—

00:13:16.775 --> 00:13:19.027
isn't that what gives
a hero's existence meaning?

00:13:19.194 --> 00:13:20.487
Philosophy from King?!

00:13:21.321 --> 00:13:25.451
In that respect, you've got a long
road to walk before you can become...

00:13:25.576 --> 00:13:26.827
the strongest hero.

00:13:28.245 --> 00:13:28.871
That's true!

00:13:28.954 --> 00:13:31.915
In other words, the pursuit
of the ideal remains.

00:13:32.374 --> 00:13:36.128
You must still have a great deal
of unrealized potential.

00:13:36.712 --> 00:13:37.796
And in that case,

00:13:38.464 --> 00:13:41.300
to say that you've reached
the limit of your growth

00:13:41.383 --> 00:13:44.261
starts to sound shallow
and arrogant, doesn't it?

00:13:44.553 --> 00:13:45.596
King...

00:13:47.556 --> 00:13:50.392
What does it take to be
the "ultimate hero"?

00:13:50.976 --> 00:13:53.020
An unflinching sense of justice?

00:13:53.437 --> 00:13:55.230
The courage to face any hardship?

00:13:55.898 --> 00:13:58.275
Until you've found the answer
to that question,

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.861
how can you say
you have time to feel bored?

00:14:02.029 --> 00:14:03.822
Those are my thoughts, anyway.

00:14:04.656 --> 00:14:06.074
Plus I read it in a manga.

00:14:06.658 --> 00:14:08.243
You blow my mind...

00:14:10.037 --> 00:14:11.330
The "ultimate hero"?

00:14:12.206 --> 00:14:14.500
Should I be thinking about
What that truly means?

00:14:16.043 --> 00:14:18.504
I think it'd make me
even more bored.

00:14:18.837 --> 00:14:21.840
If you're that bored,
wanna come play games?

00:14:22.007 --> 00:14:24.718
No, that's totally not
what I'm feeling right now.

00:14:25.093 --> 00:14:27.054
I'm numb and nothing'll change it.

00:14:27.304 --> 00:14:29.473
Don't be like that.
Let's do it.

00:14:29.681 --> 00:14:31.308
Sometimes you want to lose, right?

00:14:31.517 --> 00:14:32.726
So I'll let you lose.

00:14:34.061 --> 00:14:35.604
You can't trick me.

00:14:35.729 --> 00:14:39.441
Anyway, I wouldn't get upset
just because I lost some game.

00:14:39.942 --> 00:14:42.277
I feel totally emptied out
right now.

00:14:42.653 --> 00:14:44.404
Yeah? Okay.

00:14:44.738 --> 00:14:46.031
Tell you what—as a handicap,

00:14:46.114 --> 00:14:48.158
I'll play with just one finger
from each hand.

00:14:48.575 --> 00:14:49.535
Okay, jerkoff!

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:51.453
I'm so gonna crush
your ass this time!

00:14:54.957 --> 00:14:57.376
I never thought itd be him
that beat me...

00:15:00.128 --> 00:15:04.466
His speed and power
were exceptional.

00:15:04.967 --> 00:15:07.010
I was lucky to even get away.

00:15:07.469 --> 00:15:11.306
Martial arts designed for
Aurnan opponents were a poor match

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:13.141
against his four-legged
fighting style.

00:15:13.976 --> 00:15:15.519
That was a good lesson.

00:15:17.521 --> 00:15:19.481
This fs the freaking best!

00:15:19.606 --> 00:15:22.276
/can become so much stronger!

00:15:23.485 --> 00:15:24.444
Huh?

00:15:24.528 --> 00:15:25.362
That's...

00:15:26.196 --> 00:15:27.322
Yeah, that's him.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.992
I wont get a second chance.

00:15:31.368 --> 00:15:33.829
My body can handle it
and the pain Is gone.

00:15:34.037 --> 00:15:37.165
In fact, !m so stoked
I feel full up with power!

00:15:37.583 --> 00:15:40.419
King, it's your turn to be hunted!

00:15:41.169 --> 00:15:44.464
What will his move be
when he reacts?

00:15:45.382 --> 00:15:46.174
I've got it!

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:47.342
Get ready to die!

00:15:47.634 --> 00:15:48.594
What?

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.974
He was trying to attack you.
You know him?

00:15:54.057 --> 00:15:56.101
Nope, no idea.

00:15:57.019 --> 00:16:00.355
As if monsters weren't enough.
Now we're fighting hoodlums too?

00:16:00.439 --> 00:16:01.440
Where's it end?

00:16:01.857 --> 00:16:05.152
By the way, have you heard
what's going on?

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:06.445
I haven't.

00:16:06.904 --> 00:16:08.697
I don't know the details myself,

00:16:08.864 --> 00:16:10.532
but monsters are rampaging all over

00:16:10.741 --> 00:16:14.036
and there's a guy calling himself
a "hero hunter."

00:16:14.244 --> 00:16:15.537
It's been pretty busy.

00:16:16.079 --> 00:16:17.289
That so?

00:16:17.873 --> 00:16:20.542
The hero hunter dude
has me a bit curious...

00:16:20.709 --> 00:16:21.376
Yeah?

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:26.131
There's never been a human
who calls himself a monster before.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.384
It reminds me of when I was
calling myself a "hero"

00:16:29.509 --> 00:16:30.886
and doing my own thing.

00:16:31.678 --> 00:16:33.555
So I'm hoping he lives up
to his claim...

00:16:33.889 --> 00:16:36.558
He might even be stronger
than me, you know?

00:16:37.017 --> 00:16:37.976
I see.

00:16:38.393 --> 00:16:39.853
Hope you run into him soon.

00:16:51.365 --> 00:16:52.616
Show yourself.

00:16:54.576 --> 00:16:55.577
Who are—?

00:16:56.578 --> 00:16:57.621
There's two of them!

00:16:58.914 --> 00:17:00.332
You attacked me...

00:17:00.666 --> 00:17:03.168
So I assume you're ready to die!

00:17:09.257 --> 00:17:10.258
"Attacked"?

00:17:10.676 --> 00:17:12.344
Sounds unfriendly.

00:17:13.095 --> 00:17:16.264
I'm sure you agree,
Speed-o'-Sound Sonic,

00:17:16.348 --> 00:17:19.142
last surviving member
of the Final 44?

00:17:20.185 --> 00:17:21.353
You're from the village?

00:17:22.062 --> 00:17:25.107
We are of the Golden 37.
lam Tempest Wind.

00:17:25.732 --> 00:17:27.401
Hellfire Flame.

00:17:27.901 --> 00:17:29.736
What do you want with me?

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.071
To recruit you.

00:17:31.697 --> 00:17:33.657
Interested in doing something big?

00:17:33.991 --> 00:17:35.450
Something big?

00:17:35.575 --> 00:17:36.451
Indeed.

00:17:36.535 --> 00:17:38.787
We're planning on
taking over this little planet...

00:17:39.287 --> 00:17:42.124
...-aS monsters who
transcend humankind.

00:17:42.416 --> 00:17:44.501
There's an organization
comprised only of monsters

00:17:44.626 --> 00:17:46.628
called the Monster Association.

00:17:47.129 --> 00:17:48.755
We're members.

00:17:49.089 --> 00:17:51.550
And we're about to flip
this world on its head.

00:17:51.883 --> 00:17:53.760
Sounds like a bunch of horseshit.

00:17:54.886 --> 00:17:56.430
So where do I fit in?

00:17:57.055 --> 00:18:00.183
We want to be certain we can
take down Flashy Flash.

00:18:00.517 --> 00:18:01.476
Help us.

00:18:01.685 --> 00:18:02.811
Ridiculous.

00:18:03.186 --> 00:18:05.647
I have no obligation to you,
nor the time to play games.

00:18:05.981 --> 00:18:08.358
Get lost, unless you prefer to die.

00:18:08.775 --> 00:18:10.861
Let's give him a taste.

00:18:12.029 --> 00:18:13.947
Remember how we said
"Monster Association"?

00:18:14.656 --> 00:18:15.198
We, too...

00:18:15.991 --> 00:18:16.992
...-are monsters!

00:18:19.244 --> 00:18:20.871
You'll be a monster, that's all.

00:18:21.163 --> 00:18:24.374
It's far better than any
enhancement drug or implant.

00:18:26.668 --> 00:18:29.254
The thought of getting stronger
tempts you?

00:18:30.172 --> 00:18:31.381
This is a monster cell.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.509
All you have to do is ingest it.

00:18:34.968 --> 00:18:36.553
Here, you can have this one.

00:18:37.846 --> 00:18:40.432
The Monster Association awaits you.

00:18:45.228 --> 00:18:49.524
No matter how much I train,
I see no path to beating him.

00:18:49.858 --> 00:18:52.152
But Id pay any price
for victory over Saitama.

00:18:52.527 --> 00:18:53.612
Now that price...

00:18:54.613 --> 00:18:56.573
.../8 giving up my humanity.

00:18:57.032 --> 00:18:59.076
When I lost to him,
I felt as if there was

00:18:59.326 --> 00:19:01.203
no difference between
life and death.

00:19:01.703 --> 00:19:03.997
And I have no attachments
to my human Ife.

00:19:04.998 --> 00:19:05.957
Saitama...

00:19:06.083 --> 00:19:08.210
I've decided to be a monster.

00:19:10.212 --> 00:19:12.380
Monsters remain in some areas.

00:19:12.714 --> 00:19:15.133
We can't lift the evacuation order
just yet.

00:19:15.425 --> 00:19:17.302
It's been a hell of a day...

00:19:17.552 --> 00:19:19.888
The most formidable
is Martial Gorilla.

00:19:20.472 --> 00:19:22.849
He seems obsessed
with his own threat level

00:19:22.933 --> 00:19:25.811
and declares he'll keep fighting
until he's at "Demon."

00:19:26.019 --> 00:19:27.479
City W, huh?

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.148
Have the heroes nearby
surround the city.

00:19:30.649 --> 00:19:31.775
Not necessary.

00:19:32.192 --> 00:19:35.737
Sending in a bunch of fresh meat
will only waste resources.

00:19:35.946 --> 00:19:40.659
Zombieman?!

00:19:41.243 --> 00:19:42.494
Time to get to work.

00:19:42.577 --> 00:19:44.246
Hey! I'm not seeing any heroes!

00:19:44.371 --> 00:19:45.914
If I read this right...

00:19:46.248 --> 00:19:50.252
These attacks were masterminded
by something organized...

00:19:50.836 --> 00:19:52.587
He's not paying attention.

00:19:52.671 --> 00:19:54.798
Perhaps I could track him
back to his fair...

00:19:56.299 --> 00:19:59.010
There's a sturdy fellow...

00:19:59.219 --> 00:20:00.095
Drat...

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:01.388
He's attacking a citizen.

00:20:01.888 --> 00:20:03.974
You a pro hero, big guy?

00:20:04.307 --> 00:20:04.766
Sorry?

00:20:04.891 --> 00:20:06.268
You're a gorilla!

00:20:06.518 --> 00:20:08.019
You're a gorilla, too.

00:20:09.479 --> 00:20:12.065
What are you?
Some freelance monster?

00:20:12.149 --> 00:20:16.570
What's a freelance monster?
I'm just out buying groceries.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:17.988
You're shopping?!

00:20:18.113 --> 00:20:20.615
Like a monster pretending
to live a human life?!

00:20:20.782 --> 00:20:22.659
You're a disgrace
to gorilla monsters!

00:20:22.826 --> 00:20:25.245
I'm not sure how to
respond to that...

00:20:25.453 --> 00:20:27.289
If you're a potential enemy,

00:20:27.414 --> 00:20:29.124
you die where you stand
partially upright!

00:20:32.127 --> 00:20:33.962
Take your issues elsewhere.

00:20:36.464 --> 00:20:39.217
Changing target.
I'm following him instead...

00:20:41.011 --> 00:20:42.012
In the end,

00:20:42.304 --> 00:20:46.474
we spent the whole day
getting rid of monsters.

00:20:46.683 --> 00:20:49.561
Though of course,
that's your day job.

00:20:50.437 --> 00:20:51.479
Say, Bang...

00:20:52.063 --> 00:20:54.900
Think maybe one of
the heroes or monsters

00:20:54.983 --> 00:20:57.986
got to Garou in all the panic?

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.363
That's not what happened, Brother.

00:21:00.655 --> 00:21:03.450
I didn't train him to be weak.

00:21:04.868 --> 00:21:09.331
That's why it's my responsibility
to defeat him.

00:21:10.332 --> 00:21:11.333
Garou...

00:21:11.499 --> 00:21:15.503
Do you realize what it means
to become a monster?

00:21:16.129 --> 00:21:17.672
If you're going down into darkness,

00:21:18.173 --> 00:21:20.342
at least let it be at my hands.

00:21:22.928 --> 00:21:25.972
The sun will be setting soon...

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:29.893
We've received a vital report
from Drive Knight

00:21:30.185 --> 00:21:32.312
regarding the "enemy"
in today's events.

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:34.231
They call themselves
the "Monster Association."

00:21:34.689 --> 00:21:36.191
While their objectives are unclear,

00:21:36.316 --> 00:21:38.693
they tout themselves as our rivals

00:21:38.944 --> 00:21:42.113
and have a method for turning
humans into monsters.

00:21:42.781 --> 00:21:45.200
Their leader is
the "Monster King" Orochi.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.786
We also received the approximate
location of their lair.

00:21:48.036 --> 00:21:51.039
The location is City Z's
abandoned "ghost town."

00:21:51.373 --> 00:21:53.375
The area that was taken
by the monsters...

00:21:53.583 --> 00:21:57.629
They went through a lot of trouble
to kidnap an executive's son...

00:21:57.754 --> 00:21:59.881
Perhaps it's a sign
they want to negotiate.

00:22:00.048 --> 00:22:00.882
I agree.

00:22:00.966 --> 00:22:03.301
It's their way of saying
"don't try anything."

00:22:03.677 --> 00:22:05.345
They're probably thinking

00:22:05.428 --> 00:22:08.556
they can talk their way
out of extermination.

00:22:08.807 --> 00:22:12.686
If the ghost town monsters have
formed some sort of coalition

00:22:12.769 --> 00:22:13.728
that makes sense...

00:22:13.937 --> 00:22:16.147
In that case,
this riot by the monsters

00:22:16.273 --> 00:22:19.526
could have been their way of
staging a protest.

00:22:20.026 --> 00:22:25.407
These monsters possess
the intellect to act as a group.

00:22:25.657 --> 00:22:29.619
The likelinood that they will
reach out to us is extremely high.

00:22:29.995 --> 00:22:32.038
That could be our "in."

00:22:32.247 --> 00:22:35.625
Let's think of some sort of ruse,
then wipe them out.

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:37.919
We should hear what
they have to say first.

00:22:38.169 --> 00:22:41.589
Our primary objective remains
the rescue of the hostage.

00:22:41.715 --> 00:22:42.257
Correct.

00:22:42.382 --> 00:22:45.468
Esteemed advisor Narinki
is one our top donors.

00:22:45.719 --> 00:22:49.097
If anything happens to his son,
he could cut us off.

00:22:49.597 --> 00:22:51.016
We must rescue the boy.

00:22:51.599 --> 00:22:54.602
We received a message
from the Monster Association!

00:22:55.020 --> 00:22:58.231
We received a message
from the Monster Association!

00:22:58.315 --> 00:22:58.857
What sort of—?

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:00.900
— We received a message
— Hey!

00:23:00.984 --> 00:23:03.236
— from the Monster Association!
— Something's wrong with him.

00:23:03.320 --> 00:23:07.198
We received a message...
from the Monster Association...

00:23:07.282 --> 00:23:08.950
We received a message...

00:23:10.285 --> 00:23:14.080
We received a message
from the Monster Association.

00:23:25.216 --> 00:23:27.969
I'm sure it was a good Call
to cook this thing.

00:23:28.303 --> 00:23:32.140
Common sense says
not to eat meat like this raw.

00:23:33.224 --> 00:23:35.060
It try not to think about it.

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:40.315
You just watch your back...

00:23:41.232 --> 00:23:42.233
... Saitama!

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:45.320
AFTERWARD, SONIC GOT
A BAD CASE OF THE RUNS

00:23:45.653 --> 00:23:50.283
JUSTICE UNDER SIEGE
